    q: "Why is my True refrigerator not cooling?",
    a: "A True Manufacturing commercial refrigerator that won't hold below 41°F usually traces to one of three causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across LA restaurants, bars, and hospitality kitchens. (1) Condenser fan motor failure — the most common single True service item across all series (T-49, T-72, TPP, TSSU, TUC). Head pressure climbs, cooling capacity drops, box temperature drifts up. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock. (2) Dirty condenser coil — restaurant kitchen grease and lint accumulate on the rear-mount or top-mount condenser fins. About 25 to 30 percent of True service calls resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with condenser cleaning, no parts charge. (3) Cold rail evaporator coil fouling (TPP and TSSU prep tables specifically) — lettuce, tomato, and sauce buildup over the coil reduces heat transfer. Deep evaporator cleaning resolves about 90 percent of 'cold rail running warm' calls on True prep tables without parts replacement."
