  },
  {
    q: "What does compressor replacement cost on a True T-49 or T-72?",
    a: "True T-49 (double-door reach-in) and T-72 (triple-door reach-in) compressor replacement runs $1,400 to $2,200 all-in including EPA 608 Universal refrigerant recovery, system evacuation to deep vacuum, new compressor installation, fresh refrigerant charge (R-134a legacy or R-290 propane on post-2020 models), pressure test, and documentation. TPP and TSSU prep table compressor replacement runs $1,200 to $1,800 (smaller compressor size). TUC undercounter compressor $1,000 to $1,600. The variation reflects compressor size and refrigerant type. On year 12+ units with compressor failure, our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair walk through repair-versus-replace math with the operator — new True T-49 retail runs $5,500 to $7,500, so year 12 compressor replacement on an otherwise healthy unit is often the correct economic call."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you carry True T-Series, TPP, TSSU, TUC, and GDM parts?",
    a: "Common True service parts on our trucks for first-visit completion across LA commercial calls: condenser fan motors (most common single True repair across all series), evaporator fan motors, door gaskets for T-23, T-49, T-72, TPP, TSSU, TUC, and TG dimensions, defrost heaters (Calrod element for T-49F, T-23F freezer variants and walk-in cooler defrost), and anti-condensation heaters for TG-1S, TG-2, TG-3, and GDM glass-door merchandisers. Less common parts — specific compressor units, TXV models, full control boards — order through Parts Town and Trulaske Madison Missouri authorized distribution, 3 to 7 day standard. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair pre-order based on phone-call symptom description to compress restoration time on critical commercial calls."
  },
  {
    q: "Why is my True TG or GDM glass-door merchandiser fogging?",
    a: "Almost always anti-condensation heater failure in the glass door frame. The anti-condensation heater is a low-wattage wire embedded in the glass frame that prevents condensation on the glass surface when humid LA kitchen or bar ambient air contacts the cold glass. Year 5 to 8 typical wear curve. Symptom: glass fogs progressively, eventually drips, customer assumes gasket failure. Diagnostic: continuity test on the heater wire — open circuit confirms failure. Replacement requires partial frame disassembly. $340 to $580 typical all-in. Anti-condensation heater is the limiting factor on TG-1S, TG-2, TG-3, and GDM glass-door merchandiser lifespan."
  },
  {
    q: "Should I repair or replace a year-12 True T-49?",
    a: "Honest math we walk through with operators at the diagnostic visit. A new True T-49 reach-in retail runs $5,500 to $7,500. Repair economics at year 12: compressor replacement $1,400 to $2,200 makes sense if the rest of the system is healthy (evaporator, condenser, controls) and the door gaskets are sound or replaceable. Replacement makes sense if compressor failure is the third major repair in 18 months, if the refrigerant is R-134a legacy and a planned R-290 transition makes operational sense, or if door gaskets are showing visible degradation at multiple positions. T-49 cabinet quality is excellent — Trulaske family commercial quality — and year 12 with one major repair history typically justifies continued repair. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair tell you straight which call the math favors before any repair work begins."
  },
  {
    q: "Where can I get True parts in LA?",
    a: "True Manufacturing parts route through Parts Town authorized distribution and Trulaske Madison Missouri direct channels. Standard ship 3 to 5 day for common service parts (condenser fan motors, evaporator fan motors, door gaskets, defrost heaters, anti-condensation heaters); expedited 1 to 3 day available for service-critical parts on commercial accounts. Common True T-49, T-72, TPP, TSSU, TUC, TG, and GDM service parts stocked on our trucks for first-visit completion on most LA County hospitality calls. Less common parts (specific compressor models, full control boards, custom door panels) require special order. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair pre-order based on phone-call symptom description and dispatch coordination."
  }
