<!-- 01 INTRO — answer-first lead -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · True refrigerator not cooling</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three root causes our techs diagnose first on True T-Series.</h2>

    <p>A True Manufacturing commercial refrigerator that won't hold below 41°F usually traces to one of three root causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across LA County restaurants, bars, and hospitality kitchens. (1) Condenser fan motor failure year 5 to 9 — the most common single True service item across all series (T-49, T-72, TPP, TSSU, TUC, TG, GDM). Head pressure climbs, cooling capacity drops, box temperature drifts up. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock. (2) Dirty condenser coil — restaurant kitchen grease and lint accumulate on the rear-mount or top-mount condenser fins. About 25 to 30 percent of True service calls resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with condenser cleaning, no parts charge. (3) Cold rail evaporator coil fouling on TPP and TSSU prep tables — lettuce, tomato, sauce buildup over the coil reduces heat transfer. Deep evaporator cleaning resolves about 90 percent of "cold rail running warm" calls on True prep tables without parts replacement.</p>

    <p><strong>Important: True commercial and True Residential are the same company — the Trulaske family's True Manufacturing — but different product lines.</strong> Different parts catalogs, different service paths, different support numbers. Not two companies, and True Residential is not Middleby-owned. This page covers the Trulaske family commercial line — T-Series reach-ins, TPP and TSSU prep tables, TUC undercounter, TG and GDM glass-door merchandisers used by restaurants, bars, and hospitality operators across LA. See the broader <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/brands/true/">True Manufacturing brand pillar</a> for full lineup context.</p>

    <p><strong>$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair.</strong> BHGS Registration #A49573 and EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), plus R-290 propane certification for newer True green-refrigerant models (2020+). CSLB C-20 HVAC. BBB Accredited Business. 90-day warranty. Same-day across LA, OC, Ventura. Next-day Riverside and San Bernardino. Sister sub-services: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-cooler-not-cooling/">walk-in cooler not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/commercial-freezer-not-freezing/">commercial freezer not freezing</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/not-cooling/">generic commercial refrigeration not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/compressor-issues/">compressor issues</a>. Parent: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/">commercial refrigeration</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 DIAGNOSTIC SEQUENCE -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Five-step diagnostic on every True not-cooling call</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Cheap-first sequence across T-Series, TPP, TSSU, TUC, GDM.</h2>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Box temperature documentation.</strong> Probe at product level (not air space at ceiling) to verify current product temperature against the operator's last log entry. Establishes HACCP CCP exceedance window for California Retail Food Code 41°F compliance.</li>
      <li><strong>Identify series and refrigerant.</strong> T-49, T-72, TPP, TSSU, TUC, TG, or GDM. Rating label refrigerant (R-134a legacy or R-290 propane post-2020) determines sealed-system service certification requirement.</li>
      <li><strong>Visual condenser inspection.</strong> Rear-mount (T-23, T-49, T-72) or top-mount (TPP, TSSU, TUC) condenser. Grease, lint, dust accumulation on fins. If condenser is the diagnosis, cleaning runs $200 to $280 and resolves the call without parts on 25 to 30 percent of LA True service visits.</li>
      <li><strong>Condenser fan motor amp draw and rotation.</strong> Multimeter at fan motor terminals against rated spec, visual rotation check. Most common single True service item across all series. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock for common shaded-pole sizes.</li>
      <li><strong>TPP/TSSU cold rail evaporator inspection (prep tables only).</strong> Lettuce, tomato, sauce buildup on evaporator coil. Deep evaporator cleaning resolves 90 percent of cold rail running warm calls without parts replacement.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Most diagnostics complete in 25 to 40 minutes on-site. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair walk operators through the findings with photo documentation before any repair work begins. Sealed-system work on R-290 propane True models requires both EPA 608 Universal certification (#1346255700410) and R-290 hydrocarbon certification, which we hold and document on every True post-2020 service visit.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TOP CAUSES FREQUENCY -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · Top causes by frequency</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Across LA County True service calls.</h2>

    <p>Across LA County True Manufacturing commercial refrigerator service calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run — Sunset Strip restaurants with T-49 and T-72 reach-ins, DTLA hotel banquet kitchens with TPP and TSSU prep stations, Beverly Hills luxury hospitality with TG and GDM glass-door merchandisers, bars across West Hollywood and Hollywood with TUC undercounter back-bar storage, ghost kitchens and food trucks with TSSU and TUC compact units, sushi restaurants with TSSU-72-30M-B-ST megatop prep — the failure breakdown clusters predictably.</p>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Condenser fan motor failure (25-30% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Most common single True service item across all series. Year 5 to 9 typical wear curve. Head pressure climbs without fan circulation, cooling capacity drops, box temperature drifts up. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock for common shaded-pole motor sizes. Common across T-23, T-49, T-72, TPP, TSSU, TUC, and TG series.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Dirty condenser coil (20-25% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulate on rear-mount or top-mount condenser fins. Resolves at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning on 25 to 30 percent of True service calls, no parts charge. Standalone deep cleaning $200 to $280.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Cold rail evaporator fouling — TPP and TSSU prep tables (15-20% of TPP/TSSU calls)</h3>
      <p>Lettuce drippings, tomato juice, sauce splash, and condensation accumulate on the evaporator coil sitting above the cold rail. Heat transfer drops, cold rail drifts warm. Deep evaporator cleaning resolves 90 percent of cold rail running warm calls without parts replacement. $200 to $340 typical deep clean. TPP-44, TPP-60, TPP-67, TPP-93, TPP-119, TSSU-27, TSSU-48, TSSU-72 all share this failure pattern.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Door gasket year 5-7 (10-15% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Compression set, tearing, magnetic seal failure. Warm air infiltration, defrost cycle overwhelmed, frost buildup or temperature drift. $180 to $340 replacement covering T-23, T-49, T-72, TPP, TSSU, TUC, TG dimensions stocked on truck.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>5. Defrost heater (Calrod element) — T-49F and T-23F freezer variants (8-12% of freezer calls)</h3>
      <p>Year 5 to 8 typical wear. Calrod element open-circuited, evaporator coil ice buildup, box temperature drifts above 0°F. $380 to $580 replacement accessed via evaporator panel, 2 to 3 hour repair.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>6. Anti-condensation heater — TG and GDM glass-door merchandisers (8-12% of glass-door calls)</h3>
      <p>Anti-condensation heater wire in glass door frame open-circuited. Glass fogs progressively, eventually drips. Year 5 to 8 typical wear. $340 to $580 replacement requires partial frame disassembly. Limiting factor on TG-1S, TG-2, TG-3, and GDM lifespan.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 TRUE SERIES PATTERNS -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">04 · True series-specific service patterns</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">T-Series, TPP, TSSU, TUC, TG / GDM — different failure profiles.</h2>

    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li><strong>T-Series Reach-Ins (T-23 single-door, T-49 double-door, T-72 triple-door + F suffix freezer variants).</strong> Industry workhorse line. Condenser fan motor (most common), door gasket year 5 to 7, defrost heater Calrod 5 to 8 year on freezer F variants, compressor year 10 to 12.</li>
      <li><strong>TPP Prep Tables (sandwich/salad: TPP-44, TPP-60, TPP-67, TPP-93, TPP-119, plus -D2 storage variant).</strong> Cold rail evaporator fouling is the dominant service item. Deep evaporator clean resolves 90 percent of "cold rail warm" calls without parts.</li>
      <li><strong>TSSU Sandwich Prep Undercounter (TSSU-27, TSSU-48, TSSU-72, plus megatop sushi TSSU-72-30M-B-ST).</strong> Same cold rail diagnostic patterns as TPP series. Lower profile, often tucked under counter surfaces. Coastal salt and tight installation airflow are limiting factors.</li>
      <li><strong>TUC Undercounter (TUC-27 single-door, TUC-48 single section 2-drawer or 2-door, TUC-67 two-section, plus TUC-F freezer variants and TUC-CB chef base).</strong> Compact form factor. Coastal salt and tight installation airflow are the limiting factors. TUC-CB chef base for cooking equipment lines sees additional heat load.</li>
      <li><strong>TG and GDM Glass-Door Merchandisers (TG-1S, TG-2, TG-3 plus GDM line).</strong> Display refrigeration. Anti-condensation heater in glass frame is the limiting factor (5 to 8 year typical service life). LED interior lighting harness corrosion year 6+.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

